  "description": "XIYNOL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C85 H106 Gd9 N3 O53,C1 H4 O1,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 17 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.557-4.331 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.75-134.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd9L1(L2)2(OAc)15(OH)8(H2O)2(DMF)](CH3OH)2(H2O)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 15 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
